  "Question": "The marking line of an angled parking space is 6 m long and forms an acute angle of \\(30^\\circ\\) with the driving aisle. How many m of depth does the space occupy perpendicular to the driving aisle?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "3",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Depth \\(=6\\times\\sin30^\\circ=6\\times\\frac{1}{2}=3\\) m.\n\nAlternative method 1: Use the 30° right-triangle property\n\nDropping a perpendicular from the far endpoint of the marking line to the aisle forms a right triangle. The 6 m marking line is its hypotenuse, and the depth is the leg opposite \\(30^\\circ\\). In a right triangle, that leg is half the hypotenuse, so the depth is \\(6/2=3\\) m.",
